SECTION atomic-unit-rule
NUMBER 4.2
TITLE "Atomic unit rule"

RULE atomic-unit-principle
  GOAL
    Each promotable forensic record and each independently meaningful synthesis record
    MUST describe exactly one independently evidenced unit: one function, method, route,
    query, job, workflow node, graph edge, action, binding, DB routine, constraint,
    widget behavior, interface operation, architecture module/bounded context, or
    equivalent. A purely navigational grouping container, for example a family index,
    class overview, workflow overview, capability index, module index, or use-case
    index, MUST be marked RECORD-KIND: GROUPING-CONTAINER. It has only a title,
    navigation metadata, and an explicit member-ID list; it MUST NOT carry independent
    semantic claims, STAGING-STATUS, COVERAGE-STATUS, blueprint/handbook status,
    BLOCK-CONFIDENCE-RANK, BLOCK-EVIDENCE-PROFILE, semantic record version/fingerprint,
    or confirmation, and MUST NOT inherit any such value from children.
  END
END

RULE module-and-container-semantics
  GOAL
    A module or bounded context that states responsibility, public interfaces,
    encapsulation boundary, dependencies, invariants, or data passed is not a grouping
    container. It is an atomic semantic MOD block governed by the common synthesis
    header, material CLMs, reciprocal references, coverage, semantic
    version/fingerprint, and confirmation. Module indexes MAY remain purely navigational
    grouping containers. A CAP is the governed capability container defined in §2.6 and
    §3.2: it may carry its own claim-backed governance metadata, but it remains
    non-promotable and never inherits member evidence or coverage. Serialized files are
    containers. A whole export MUST NOT be represented as one component. A container SRC
    is C-COVERED only when its child-enumeration claim is complete for the pinned
    snapshot and every child coverage row is terminally covered or exactly excluded; it
    never inherits a child evidence rank/profile and never requires an aggregate
    promotable CMP. A container with no children requires an evidence-backed zero-child
    enumeration claim.
  END
END

SECTION source-inventory
NUMBER 4.3
TITLE "Source inventory denominator — `10-SOURCE-INVENTORY.md`"

GOAL
  One record exists per concrete source unit.
END

ENUM DISCOVERY-METHOD
  filesystem
  AST
  route registry
  DB catalog
  export explosion
  runtime
  operator-approved manifest
  other
END

ENUM COVERAGE-SUMMARY
  C-COVERED
  C-PARTIAL
  C-GAP
  C-EXCLUDED
  Mixed
END

ENUM INVENTORY-KIND
  files
  symbols
  routes
  RPC handlers
  jobs
  queries
  tables
  views
  triggers
  stored functions/procedures
  generated columns
  constraints
  configuration keys and feature flags
  workflow containers
  nodes
  edges
  pages
  widgets
  actions
  bindings
  queues/events
  files/storage contracts
  external interfaces
END

FIELD SOURCE-INVENTORY-RECORD
  kind                                    -> string required
  concrete-coordinate                     -> string required
  parent-container-src                    -> string required
  source-fingerprint-snapshot-src-version -> string required
  discovery-method                        -> DISCOVERY-METHOD required
  scope-summary                           -> string required
  environment-runtime-state               -> string required
  traversal-tracks                        -> string required
  canonical-owner                         -> string required
  disposition-summary                     -> string required
  mappings                                -> string required
  frontier-references                     -> string required
  coverage-rows                           -> string required
  coverage-summary                        -> COVERAGE-SUMMARY required
  claims                                  -> string required
END

RULE source-versioning
  GOAL
    Each source fingerprint/snapshot is an immutable SRC version. A changed source
    creates a new version linked by supersession; it does not overwrite prior snapshot
    state. Scope, disposition, and coverage authority live in the scope-specific rows in
    16-SOURCE-COVERAGE.md; inventory summaries are derived. A Candidate scope row is
    temporary and included in closure until changed by an approved scope decision.
    Approved-Excluded requires exact units, rationale, risk, approver, date, and DEC ID.
    Wildcards alone cannot identify exclusions at closure.
  END
END

RULE inventory-absence-proof
  GOAL
    Inventory MUST cover, where applicable, the declared inventory kinds. Absence of a
    kind MUST be proven by an inventory-backed enumerator record specifying inspected
    roots/catalogs, method, snapshot, result count zero, limitations, and CLM evidence.
    An empty section or zero rows without this proof is invalid.
  END
END

SECTION traversal-frontier
NUMBER 4.4
TITLE "Traversal frontier — `11-TRAVERSAL-FRONTIER.md`"

GOAL
  Every discovered traversal boundary MUST create exactly one FRT record, including a
  boundary recognized as terminal, duplicate, excluded, or already mapped at discovery
  time. Immediate recognition MAY create the record directly in its terminal state, but
  MUST NOT omit it. Every discovered but not yet terminal traversal boundary remains
  open until terminally disposed.
END

ENUM FRONTIER-DISCOVERY-METHOD
  call
  import
  route
  graph edge
  query reference
  DB firing
  config gate
  runtime
  other
END

ENUM FRONTIER-STATE
  Open
  Traversed
  Terminal-Mapped
  Terminal-Excluded
  Terminal-Duplicate
  Terminal-Human-Blocked
  Superseded
END

FIELD FRONTIER-RECORD
  origin-invocation-cluster-pov-track        -> string required
  from-src-cmp                               -> string required
  target-concrete-coordinate-or-resolution-rule -> string required
  target-src                                 -> string required
  discovery-method                           -> FRONTIER-DISCOVERY-METHOD required
  depth                                      -> int required
  snapshot-fingerprint                       -> string required
  state                                      -> FRONTIER-STATE required
  disposition-evidence                       -> string required
  child-frontier-ids                         -> string required
  closing-invocation                         -> string required
END

RULE frontier-terminality
  GOAL
    Depth bounds create open frontier records; they do not silently terminate traversal.
    Every frontier MUST be terminal for Exit A. Terminal-Human-Blocked remains a coverage
    gap or partial unless the underlying unit is separately approved as excluded.
  END
END

SECTION source-coverage
NUMBER 4.5
TITLE "Scope-specific source coverage — `16-SOURCE-COVERAGE.md`"

GOAL
  One row exists per immutable SRC version by persona/owner by track by environment by
  snapshot scope. Rows are disjoint within a subgroup; a source participating in several
  tracks has separate rows and is counted once in each declared track report, while the
  aggregate unique-SRC report deduplicates by SRC version.
END

ENUM COVERAGE-SCOPE
  In-Scope
  Candidate
  Approved-Excluded
END

ENUM COVERAGE-DISPOSITION
  Unmapped
  Mapped
  Superseded
  Retired
  Approved-Excluded
  Human-Blocked
END

FIELD SOURCE-COVERAGE-ROW
  cov-id                          -> string required
  src-version                     -> string required
  persona-owner                   -> string required
  track                           -> string required
  environment                     -> string required
  snapshot                        -> string required
  scope                           -> COVERAGE-SCOPE required
  disposition                     -> COVERAGE-DISPOSITION required
  c-status                        -> string required
  exclusion-dec                   -> string required
  mappings                        -> string required
  frontier-ticket-claim-evidence  -> string required
END

RULE coverage-row-identity
  GOAL
    The COV ID is deterministically derived from the complete immutable scope tuple and
    MUST be unique for it; duplicate tuple rows are invalid. The row, not the inventory
    summary, is the arithmetic input.
  END
END

SECTION supersession-tombstones
NUMBER 4.6
TITLE "Stable supersession and tombstones"

GOAL
  Records are never silently deleted. A renamed record retains its ID when identity is
  proven.
END

FIELD SUPERSESSION-TOMBSTONE
  record-version           -> int required
  supersedes               -> string required
  superseded-by            -> string required
  tombstone                -> string required
  tombstone-reason-decision -> string required
END

RULE tombstone-rules
  GOAL
    A split, merge, or semantic replacement uses the declared supersession block.
    Tombstones preserve old IDs, incoming references, and snapshot lineage. Validators
    reject references to tombstones unless the referencing block explicitly records
    historical use.
  END
END
